    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Catholic miners founded Rose Bar’s church in 1852, and after the town was abandoned, the building was moved to Smartsville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://smartsvillehistoricchurch.org/local-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Timbuctoo, once Yuba County’s largest mining town in 1855, boasted a church, theater, and Wells Fargo office, now a restored historic site.",
